{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1787250853049168002,"compiled_state":{"alias":"surah-laminate-partridge","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":4,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"cd0cf25aa12b502389f0b4cba3f2999e7013b7949e0b74fb79c599fbae92f838","event_uuid":"bd4058fd-acb0-4bcb-8957-643aaab6c655","position":{"commit_sha":"e707084e82a5e8c5402ccca705aaf8a8208690c4","position":"1787250767449980001-bd4058fd-acb0-4bcb-8957-643aaab6c655"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"d52782eb616fa78820af02f02cc8da74aeb7354b6fbcb58dfe069b76a6e55ca2","event_uuid":"9f88ffcc-d631-4f2a-8969-22de4b8eb36f","position":{"commit_sha":"92462676cb8bc5d666409e2b373fd88630006f50","position":"1787250803291983001-9f88ffcc-d631-4f2a-8969-22de4b8eb36f"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"c37869183a629d52953c5e381f8681925695975d3007ec5d58ce82fcfd8925c3","event_uuid":"5d1c03db-57c2-457e-9759-bb562e15f782","position":{"commit_sha":"e961e2ba994ec43769b7ea0e94f03c9db4275848","position":"1787250810881823001-5d1c03db-57c2-457e-9759-bb562e15f782"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"cafecf622630ec81f32c83b9135b3ae69c822ede0aa2d58ffd03876a75c66171","event_uuid":"67dfecdb-54c4-464c-9238-60202a848d3d","position":{"commit_sha":"fc129ede5021c5ff04bc9d328ae0ec2cdd46636c","position":"1787250853049168001-67dfecdb-54c4-464c-9238-60202a848d3d"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787250767449980001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"9f88ffcc-d631-4f2a-8969-22de4b8eb36f","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"054b-790b-d8e8-4aa3"},{"link_uuid":"5d1c03db-57c2-457e-9759-bb562e15f782","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"bd21-f725-0030-47ef"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nrebar is a concurrency-heavy project (multi-process writers over a git-backed store, file locks, detached children, CI-level push contention), which makes it both the ideal dogfood target and the worst case for trigger over-fire. Measured over the last 300 main commits: the committed high-precision tier fires on 14% of diffs; the noisy tier (`.lock`, `retry`, `Popen`, `fork`, …) adds a further 21%. Three of the four traced corpus bugs (`fine-wisteria-solenodon` via `index.lock`, `fervid-boring-python` via `retry`, `eclectic-spotted-barb` via `Popen`/`start_new_session`) trigger only through noisy-tier vocabulary — so for THIS repo the noisy tier is load-bearing, and per the parent epic's decided design it lives in the project overlay, not the committed list. Nothing currently documents the two-layer trigger design for other projects to copy.\n\n## Approach\n\nTwo deliverables. (1) Add a `concurrency` entry to the `code_review` section of this repo's `.rebar/criteria_routing.json` using the project-extension mechanism delivered by the prerequisite story: `trigger_tokens` `[\".lock\", \"retry\", \"Popen\", \"start_new_session\", \"setsid\", \"fork\", \"index.lock\", \"stage_and_commit\", \"push_tickets_branch\", \"refs/reconciler/\"]` and `applies_to` `[\"**/_store/**\", \"**/lock*\", \"**/enrich_drain*\", \".github/workflows/**\"]`. (2) Document the two-layer trigger design in `docs/llm-framework.md` adjacent to the existing code-review routing material (the routing/prompt/eval pointer block around docs/llm-framework.md:661): the committed high-precision tier and its survey grounding, the project noisy tier and how a project adds vocabulary, the measured fire-rate tradeoff (14% vs +21% on this repo), and this repo's entry as the worked example. Positive rationale: the dogfood entry is load-bearing (it is what makes the corpus bugs trigger here) and doubles as documentation-by-example, the same way this repo's `project.portability` and `project.engine-layer-enforcement` entries demo the plan-review project overlay.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `.rebar/criteria_routing.json` — the `code_review.concurrency` project entry.\n- `docs/llm-framework.md` — the two-layer trigger section.\n- `tests/unit/test_criteria_overlay.py` — the config-effect case below.\n\n## Testing\n\nConfig-effect contrast (shared test-design standard §6), unit tier: one test proving the project entry changes behavior through the REAL read path — a fixture diff containing `index.lock` (a project token deliberately absent from the committed high-precision list) fires the `concurrency` overlay when `content_triggered_overlays` runs with `repo_root` = this checkout, and does NOT fire under committed-only routing (no `repo_root` / a bare tmp root). A test that only parsed the JSON would miss the read-but-miswired class; this asserts the observable outcome differs across the two routing states.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `.rebar/criteria_routing.json` carries the `code_review.concurrency` entry with the tokens and globs listed in the Approach; checked by reading the file.\n- [ ] Config-effect test: a diff containing `index.lock` fires `concurrency` under this repo's effective routing and not under committed-only routing; checked by `pytest tests/unit/test_criteria_overlay.py`.\n- [ ] `docs/llm-framework.md` documents the two tiers, the fire-rate measurement, and how a project adds vocabulary, using this repo's entry as the worked example; checked by reading the section.\n- [ ] `make lint`, `make typecheck`, and the targeted pytest module pass.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":".rebar/criteria_routing.json","reason":"code_review.concurrency project entry (noisy-tier tokens + globs)"},{"path":"docs/llm-framework.md","reason":"two-layer trigger design documentation"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_criteria_overlay.py","reason":"config-effect contrast test"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["depends_on","054b-790b-d8e8-4aa3"],["depends_on","bd21-f725-0030-47ef"],["parent","292f-57d1-e554-486f"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"292f-57d1-e554-486f","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"5756-ef1a-68ab-4ba4","ticket_type":"story","title":"Dogfood: rebar project trigger vocabulary + two-layer trigger docs","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["bd4058fd-acb0-4bcb-8957-643aaab6c655","9f88ffcc-d631-4f2a-8969-22de4b8eb36f","5d1c03db-57c2-457e-9759-bb562e15f782","67dfecdb-54c4-464c-9238-60202a848d3d"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787250853049168002,"uuid":"327da97c-0394-4761-b5db-6ab40e7aca70"}